From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Subject: ARM: dts: qcom: ipq8064: align TSENS qfprom cells

The IPQ8064 qfprom provider exposes 4-byte words.  The TSENS calibration
cells are currently described as 11 bytes, which makes the nvmem core warn
while it internally rounds the raw read length up to 12 bytes anyway:

  nvmem qfprom12: cell calib raw len 11 unaligned to nvmem word size 4
  nvmem qfprom12: cell calib_backup raw len 11 unaligned to nvmem word size 4

Describe both cells with the aligned raw length expected by qfprom.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-ipq8064.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-ipq8064.dtsi
@@ -520,10 +520,10 @@
 				reg = <0xc0 0x4>;
 			};
 			tsens_calib: calib@400 {
-				reg = <0x400 0xb>;
+				reg = <0x400 0xc>;
 			};
 			tsens_calib_backup: calib_backup@410 {
-				reg = <0x410 0xb>;
+				reg = <0x410 0xc>;
 			};
 		};
 
